      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "led_driver",
        "description": "PT4115-based high-power LED constant-current buck driver for a single 1W LED load from the external VIN_12V_24V rail. This module owns the switching power stage, current regulation loop, LED current path, and dimming/control interface. VIN is taken directly from the external input rail; SW is the switching node for the external inductor/diode/current path; CSN senses LED current through an external low-side current-sense network referenced to GND to set the target 350mA operating current; DIM is exposed as the brightness control / enable-style interface and may be tied to a fixed operating state or driven by an external PWM/analog dimming source added later. The exposed LED output ports represent the controlled load current path for the downstream LED connection, and the current regulation depends on the passive power-stage and sense components that are not instantiated in Phase 0. EP and GND belong to the common ground/thermal return domain and require low-impedance grounding and high-current return routing discipline around the switching and sense paths.",
        "id": "led_driver"
      },
      {
        "type": "Component",
        "refdes": "U1",
        "part_number": "PT4115",
        "description": "High-power LED constant-current driver",
